paragraphs:
Seven founders left OpenAI to take a safer track;
Then built in checks upon themselves, should judgment ever crack.
Five trustees, paid $400,000 yearly, cannot own a share;
Their Long-Term Benefit Trust must keep humanity in its care.

One profitless Class T share names four board directors;
Class F names three, with 50.1%—the founders’ vote protector.
So money does not steer each seat or choose each final say;
The people holding special shares can point the boardroom’s way.

